// event: completion A A.x
// concurrent: completion A A.x; completion B B.v
// note: the same lock order through file roots (TASTy's): A.x in file A needs B.v in file B, which needs Q.p in file A, a chain x -> v -> p. With a root per fact or per pair no cycle; with a root per file, reader A holds file A inside x while it waits for file B, and reader B holds file B inside v and asks for file A to complete Q: a false cycle under RAISE, an abort and retry under VICTIM
// file: A
class Int {}
class A { def x = M.m.v }
object Q { def p: Int }
object M { def m = B }
// file: B
object B { def v = N.n.p }
object N { def n = Q }
